* System calls, binary images\nand processes
** System call
*** C function exposing an OS service
*** Software interrupt (svc on ARM)
*** Syscall number in a register
*** Arguments via registers or stack
*** Calling convention fixed by the ABI
*** User-space stub in the libc
**** glibc, uClibc, bionic, musl
*** Standard API: POSIX
*** Higher-level wrappers
**** fopen(), fread(), pthread_create()
*** man <section> term
**** 2 = syscalls, 3 = library
** Binary image
*** Source + headers -> compiler -> .o
*** Linker merges .o and static libraries
*** Executable format: ELF, PE, ECOFF
*** Sections: .text .data .bss .debug
*** Three address kinds
**** Relative (offset in .o)
**** Absolute (after loading)
**** Symbolic (printf, .L2)
** Process
*** Execution context
**** Code, registers (PC, SP)
*** Memory context
**** Globals, locals, constants
*** Logical resources
**** File descriptors, IPC objects
*** Hierarchy
**** Root process, parent, children
**** Threads share the process
*** Address space
**** Code, Data, BSS, Heap, Stack
**** Stack grows down, heap grows up
@endmindmap
